<DocsLayout title="batze docs — Introduction" description="Introduction to batze: open-source invoicing, projects, and client email you can self-host.">
  <h1>Introduction</h1>
  <p>
    Welcome to the batze docs. batze is an open-source tool for <strong>invoicing, projects, and client email</strong>,
    built to run on your own server.
  </p>
  <p>
    It's a Node.js and Nuxt app. Head to the <a href="/docs/quickstart">Quick start</a> to try it with Docker, or the
    <a href="/docs/self-hosting">self-hosting guide</a> to run a proper copy.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-batze-does">What batze does</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Swiss-ready <strong>invoicing</strong> with QR-bills and VAT</li>
    <li><strong>Projects</strong> and time tracking, billable straight to an invoice</li>
    <li>Client <strong>email</strong>, kept right next to the work it relates to</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="status">Project status</h2>
  <p>
    batze is built in the open and still evolving — it started as a learning project and grew into something usable.
    These docs grow alongside it, so expect a few gaps for now.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
